{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Gather to Me.</b> This is a reply to your complaint, that you said, ״I am not able, I alone, to bear them.״ And where were the first elders? Did they not also sit with them in Egypt, as it says (Exodus 3) ״Go and gather the elders of Israel״? Rather, they died in the fire of Tav'eirah; and they were fit for that from Sinai, as it is written ״and they saw the Elohim״ (Exodus 24) — for they behaved with levity, like one who bites his bread while speaking in the presence of the king, and this is ״and they ate and drank״ — and the Holy One, blessed be He, did not wish to bring mourning at the giving of the Torah, so He exacted it from them here (Tanḥuma)." "<b>whom you know, that they, etc.</b> Those whom you recognize — who were appointed as officers over them in Egypt under crushing labor, and who had compassion on them and were beaten on their account, as it says ״and the officers of the children of Israel were beaten״ (Exodus 5) — now they shall be appointed to greatness, just as they suffered in their affliction (see Sifrei)." "<b>And you shall take them.</b> Take them with words: ״Fortunate are you, that you have been appointed as leaders over the children of the Omnipresent.״" "<b>And they shall stand there with you.</b> So that Israel will see and treat them with greatness and honor, and say: These are beloved, who entered with Moshe to hear the utterance from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:24.328486636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}